{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"newrich-discreet-nettlefish","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context / Problem\nOn 2026-11-21, 4 review-bot autodeploys in a row interrupted reviews in progress, at 06:38, 08:03, 09:03 and 10:03 PST. Each happened after the deploy used up `DEPLOY_DEFER_MAX` (2400 s) with 1-2 reviews in progress (`AUTODEPLOY_REVIEW_INTERRUPT bound-exceeded`). `rebar-autodeploy-review-interrupts-bound-exceeded` went to ALARM at 09:05 PST and back to OK at 09:08 PST. The 10:06 count missed a second ALARM by about 2 minutes.\n\nThe bot stays busy because reviews stall silently until `REVIEW_TIMEOUT_SECONDS` = 1200. On 11-21 about 10 reviews hit that limit, against 29 votes; on 11-20 it was about 2. Normal reviews take about 2-5 minutes. The timed-out review of I53d60ec (05:55:50-06:15:50 PST) logged nothing for 20 minutes: no LLM call, no keepalive, no git output. The same day the bot logged 20 \"write lock still held\" lines, 93 git maintenance timeouts, and 15 `gate-scratch/reviewbot-… No such file` errors from retries pointing at scratch folders that a container recreate had removed. Each recreate then waits out the 1260 s stop grace period, and the killed reviews are retried and are in progress again before the next merge's deploy, giving a cycle of about 60 minutes.\n\nThis class recurs: greasy-plucky-piranha (closed) covers the August and 09-01/09-02 firings, and unskillful-supportive-lion (closed) raised the limit. Raising the limit does not address the silent stalls.\n\nThe cause of the stall is not identified. Hypotheses to test: waiting on the tickets-store lock; clone or snapshot I/O stuck behind git maintenance; a step before the LLM call stuck with no timeout.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] The step the stalled reviews are blocked in is identified with log evidence from the box, and recorded on this ticket.\n- [ ] Each review step before the LLM call logs when it starts and has its own timeout well under 1200 s.\n- [ ] A retry after a container recreate never refers to a scratch folder from the previous container.\n- [ ] Over a burst of at least 5 review-bot deploys, there are no bound-exceeded interrupts and 1 or fewer review timeouts per day, measured from the autodeploy and bot journals.","id":"688f-060e-c96c-4484","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"Reviews stall silently until the 1200 s cap, so every review-bot autodeploy spends the 2400 s deferral and kills in-flight reviews"},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1795380399479558001,"uuid":"c0b54a5c-cb60-44cc-962b-074c014d5909"}